Gift giving is a common form of non-market exchange within small-scale societies. Which of the following statements is true concerning this sort of exchange?;The primary motivation for this form of economic exchange in small-scale societies is not economic but social.;It usually results in an inequality in the distribution of wealth within the community.;It is better to receive gifts from others because it results in your personal enrichment and increased political power.;None of the above
The most common form of exchange in non-market economies between friendly small-scale societies is ____ .;face to face barter;gift giving;dumb barter;the sale of goods using general purpose money as a medium of exchange
According to this tutorial, the crucial difference between gifts and sales is that ____ .;gifts create and strengthen social relationships while sales usually do not;sales are more efficient than gifts in exchanging goods and services;more kinds of things can be exchanged by selling;gifts are decorated with bow knot
Which of the following things are usually considered to be important gifts in small-scale societies with non-market economies?;all of the above;none of the above;women and children;songs, dances, and speeches
Which of the following statements is true of reciprocal gift exchanges in all societies?;Participants in a gift exchange agree to receive a gift and repay it with another.;Reciprocal exchanges usually redistribute the wealth of a society in a way that causes some people to become richer than others.;Reciprocity requires that a gift be returned that has close to the same economic value.;None of the above
