The relative social position of someone in a group or in society is referred to as a _______ .;status;role;neither of the above.;rank
The part our society expects us to play in a given status is referred to as a _____ ?;role;caste;varna;job
Ascribed statuses .... ?;are acquired by birth;are acquired by both birth and achievement;do not exist in the real world - they are only theoretical;are acquired by choice

medium
Which of the following are characteristic of non-market economies?;none of the above;the use of money as a means of exchange;the ability to accumulate vast amounts of capital;highly complex economic interactions that are ultimately international in their scale
Which of the following statements is true concerning non-market economies?;They are typically found in small-scale, isolated societies.;There usually is a high level of technological knowledge.;Large-scale collaboration on subsistence jobs is common.;all of the above
If, after several minutes of negotiation, you agree to trade three music CD's with a friend for his used copy of the textbook needed in your cultural anthropology class, it would be an example of ____ .;barter;dumb barter;gift exchange;cartelization
