Which of the following statements is true of non-market economies?;They can only survive in isolation from the market economies of large-scale societies.;Most small-scale societies today still have thriving non-market economies.;Large-scale societies are beginning to give up their market economies in favor of non-market ones.;None of the above
Proprietary deed has been strongly supported by ____ ?;the U.S. and Canadian national cultures, which are European in origin;most Native American cultures in the 19th century and earlier;both of the above;none of the above
Which of the following would fit the definition of negative reciprocity in North America today?;selling flashlight batteries at triple the normal price during a prolonged blackout caused by a widespread electrical power failure;buying lunch at an inexpensive fast food restaurant and paying for it with money;none of the above;all of the above
Which of the following were intended functions of the Kwakiutl potlatch ceremonies in the 19th century?;to celebrate major life events in a family;to dispose of worthless surplus property that could not be bartered or sold to others;to reinforce the fact that no one had the right to special economic and ceremonial privileges;all of the above
Which of the following things resulted from international commerce during the last two centuries?;There has been an enormous redistribution of wealth to the industrialized nations located mostly in the Northern Hemisphere;There has been a redistribution of wealth from the rich nations to the poor ones so that the economic disparity between them is now less than it was two centuries ago.;There is now a balance in trade between the richest and the poorest nations in the world.;None of the above
Age-based categories are referred to by anthropologists as ____ .;age grades;age groups;age clads;age phases
Which of the following statements is true?;It is common for people to have multiple overlapping statuses and roles.;Social group membership usually gives us a set of statuses and role tags that make it more difficult for people to know what to expect from each other.;neither of the above;both of the above
The Girl Scouts is an example of _____ .;all of the above;a voluntary association;an age-based group;a gender-based group
Which of the following is an achieved status?;both;being a general in the U.S. Army;being a well recognized and accomplished movie actor;none
Voluntary associations are usually based on ______ status.;achieved;ascribed;both achieved and ascribed;none of the above
