What normally functions as rudimentary credit institutions in non-market economies?;social ties including kinship;local banks that lend money at low interest rates;nothing serves the function of a credit institution in these societies - each family must fend for itself.;Social banking
The concept of ownership in which land and other property rights are restricted by the overriding rights vested in the community as a whole is called ____ .;usufruct;vivaldi;proprietary deed;jurisprudence
