Which of the following statements is true of commerce between small-scale societies in the past?;It involved more institutionalized balanced reciprocity than is found generally in the international trade system today.;It involved far less social gain than is the case of international trade today.;Neither of the above statements is true because there was no commerce between small-scale societies in the past.;None of the above statements is true
